// CHRONOSTASIS - TEMPORAL DISTORTION
// The first second at a clock lasting forever
// Subjective time dilation from perceptual editing during attention shifts
// By Claude, exploring elastic duration

setcps(120/60/4) // 120 BPM - constant "real time" (never changes)

// STRUCTURAL SECTIONS (via angle bracket alternation):
// Cycles 0-3: Baseline time (normal perception)
// Cycles 4-5: First chronostasis event (transition stretches)
// Cycles 6-11: Multiple shift events (temporal elasticity at boundaries)
// Cycles 12-17: Accumulated distortion (frequent transitions)
// Cycles 18-23: Maximum elasticity (time wobbling)
// Cycles 24-29: Return to baseline (stabilizing)
// Cycles 30-35: Temporal ambiguity (final uncertainty)

stack(
  // METRONOME PULSE - unwavering temporal reference (always 120 BPM)
  // This represents "real time" - never wavers, never changes
  sound("click*4")
    .gain("<0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.6 0.5 0.4 0.3 0.2 0.1 0 0>")
    .pan(0.5),

  // PRIMARY PAD - time-stretching during transitions
  // Normal speed, then slows at transitions (subjectively stretched), then catches up
  note("<[0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11]!0.5 [0 4 6 11]!0.5 [0 4 6 11] [2 6 9 13] [2 6 9 13] [2 6 9 13] [4 7 11 14] [4 7 11 14] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11]!0.5 [2 6 9 13] [2 6 9 13] [4 7 11 14] [4 7 11 14]!0.5 [0 4 6 11] [2 6 9 13]!0.5 [4 7 11 14] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [2 6 9 13] [2 6 9 13] [4 7 11 14] [4 7 11 14] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11] [0 4 6 11]>")
